<title>USA: NYSE Unavailables - UNUM, Northwestern Public Service, D.R. Horton. [CORRECTED 00:05 6/2]</title>
<headline>NYSE Unavailables - UNUM, Northwestern Public Service, D.R. Horton. [CORRECTED 00:05 6/2]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Wednesday that UNUM Corp, Northwestern Public Service (corrects from Northern States Power Co) and D.R. Horton Inc were not available for after-hours trading because of news.</p>
<p>Unum on Wednesday reported fourth-quarter earnings per share of $0.66, compared to $0.85 for the same period in 1995. But the company said its operating income per share for the 1996 quarter was $1.10, compared to $0.96 for the fourth quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>The exchange said Corimon SACA also was unavailable.</p>
</text>
